From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:17:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08142/11362] [outer-loop] REPRODUCE defect C: CEGIS refinement
 leaks the held-out acceptance rows

Reproduce-only phase; no shipped behaviour changed. Every number produced by calling the
shipped functions, not by reading them. Exact law validated 270/270 and delivered into the
prompt STRING 270/270; leak is TOTAL on 9 of 13 real roster windows in the prefix-perfect arm.
Two adjacent defects found: 4 of 13 games have a structurally undecidable acceptance gate
(a PERFECT engine scores 0.0), and today's induce prompt already shows the whole held-out
tail with answers. Recommends design (ii) with three companions; rejects design (i) on
measured grounds. Full detail: results/outer_loop_arc_cegis_purity_leak_20260803.json

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
